R60 path is shorted by its own connection.\", \"expected\": \"The second LED of the dual indicator should span a real voltage difference, with its anode on a driven rail or signal and its cathode on the resistor, to indicate state.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)\"}], \"impact\": \"The ESTOP_OUT status indicator LED never lights, so the e-stop state indication is lost.\", \"confidence\": 0.4}]}",
